==English==
{{was wotd|2018|July|11}}

===Etymology===
[[File:European Parliament Strasbourg 2015-10-28 02.jpg|thumb|The [[hemicycle]] of the [[European Parliament]] in [[Strasbourg]], [[France]]. The European Parliament exercises the [[lawmaking]] function of the [[European Union]], and thus contributes towards the EU’s acquis.]]

Shortened from {{m|en|acquis communautaire}}: {{der|en|fr|acquis||that which has been acquired or obtained}} + {{m|fr|communautaire||of the community}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/aˈkiː/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ɑˈki/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|ac|quis|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|law}} The [[accumulated#Adjective|accumulated]] [[legislation]], [[legal]] [[act#Noun|acts]], and [[court#Noun|court]] [[decision]]s which constitute the [[total#Adjective|total]] [[body]] of [[European Union]] [[law]].
# {{lb|en|international law}} The accumulated legislation and decisions of any international [[community]].
#* {{quote-book|author=Gerhard Erasmus|author2=Trudi Hartzenberg|author3=Paul Kalenga|chapter=Patterns of African Regional Integration: The Tripartite and Continental Free Trade Areas|editors=Achim Gutowski [''et al.'']|title=Africa’s Progress in Regional and Global Economic Integration&nbsp;– Towards Transformative Regional Integration|series=African Development Perspectives Yearbook 2015/16|seriesvolume=18|location=Zürich|publisher={{w|LIT Verlag}}|year=2016|page=87|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=KjOSDQAAQBAJ&pg=PA87|isbn=978-3-643-90523-9|passage='''Acquis''' is a French term meaning "that which has been agreed". In the context of the Tripartite Free Trade Agreement (TFTA) means that the negotiations should start from the point at which {{...}} the COMESA, EAC and SADC trade negotiations have reached. Tariff negotiations and the exchange of tariff concessions would be among Member/Partner States of the Tripartite FTA that have no preferential arrangements in place between them. This will both preserve the '''acquis''' and build on it.}}

